{"episodes":{"207076":"Low pressure tracking across the Great Lakes region swung a cold front through West Virginia on October 21st. With freezing levels lowered for this time of year, a small pocket of showers grew vertically into thunderstorms capable of producing large hail across northeast West Virginia. Just before 8 PM that evening, several reports from the public and trained spotters across Lewis and Barbour Counties observed hailstones on the order of 1 to 1.25 inches within these storms. Activity quickly moved out of the forecast area after this instance due to the progression of the cold front.","207575":"A cold front sparked widespread showers, with one notable thunderstorm rapidly traversing the Tennessee Valley, producing hail up to 1 inch.","208000":"On the evening of October 21st, a waterspout developed over Lake Erie as a cold front crossed the lake. A few hours later, as a trough crossed Lake Erie, showers and thunderstorms along the trough became strong, causing a 34 knot wind gust at the Barcelona Harbor C-Man station.","208440":"Thunderstorms moving through Saginaw Bay and southern Lake Huron produced wind gusts in excess of 40 knots.","208441":"Thunderstorms moving through Lake St. Clair and the Detroit River produced wind gusts in excess of 45 knots."},"events":[{"begin":"2025-10-21T18:00Z","county":"Loudon","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2025-10-21T18:00Z","endLat":35.7,"endLon":-84.27,"episode":207575,"id":1294607,"injuries":0,"lat":35.7,"location":"1.49 SSE Piney","lon":-84.27,"magnitude":0.88,"source":"Public","state":"TN","type":"Hail","wfo":"MRX"},{"begin":"2025-10-21T18:04Z","county":"Blount","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2025-10-21T18:07Z","endLat":35.82,"endLon":-84.07,"episode":207575,"id":1294608,"injuries":0,"lat":35.82,"location":"0.56 E Pumpkin Center","lon":-84.07,"magnitude":0.75,"source":"Trained Spotter","state":"TN","type":"Hail","wfo":"MRX"},{"begin":"2025-10-21T18:14Z","county":"Knox","damagePropert